course: dictionary
lesson: 12466
title: Final and settled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Definitive means final and settled, so that nobody can argue with it or change it. «The judge gave a definitive answer: the match was a draw.» Once the judge has decided, that is the end of the matter.
explain: Definitive can also mean the best or most complete version of something. «This is the definitive guide to sharks» means it is the one book you would trust most. Clues like final, settled, best or complete tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Scientists are careful with this word. They say results are «not yet definitive» when more tests are needed before anyone can be sure. If you see «not yet» in front of it, the answer is still open.
fact: Definitive means final and settled, so nobody can argue with it.
fact: «Definitive proof» is proof that settles a question beyond doubt.
fact: «The definitive guide» means the most complete and most trusted guide.
fact: Definitive is an adjective. Its comparative form is more definitive.
fact: Scientists say «not yet definitive» when results still need checking.
exercise: «The referee's decision was definitive, and no one could change it.» What does definitive mean here? | Hard to read | *Final and settled | Quick and noisy | Written in pencil
exercise: «This is the definitive guide to dinosaurs.» What does definitive suggest? | A very short book | A book that is free | *The best and most complete version | A book for babies
exercise: Scientists say «the results are not yet definitive». What does this mean? | The results are perfect | The results are wrong and must be thrown away | *The answer is not settled yet | The results are written in another language
test: «Her proof was definitive, so the class believed her.» What is the closest meaning to definitive? | Loud | Settled and beyond doubt | Funny | *Unfinished
test: «Which is the definitive list of the planets?» What does definitive mean in this sentence? | A list that is too long | *The most trusted and complete | A list written in sand | The list with the most words
exam: «The definitive answer ended the argument.» Swap your meaning into the sentence. Which meaning fits best? | Wet and grey | Very hungry | Very quiet | *Final and settled
